00:01:54.500 --> 00:01:57.160
It says it's a world of dreams and adventure,

00:01:57.160 --> 00:02:00.000
as well as love, hope,
and pure righteous amusement.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:03.080
What the hell? That's piling it on too thick.

00:02:07.410 --> 00:02:09.250
Let's see...

00:02:09.250 --> 00:02:12.660
"Regular day pass" "Reserved ticket"
"Regular day pass," "reserved ticket,"
"annual pass," "premium ticket"...

00:02:12.660 --> 00:02:15.250
"Annual pass" "Premium ticket"
"Regular day pass," "reserved ticket,"
"annual pass," "premium ticket"...

00:02:15.250 --> 00:02:19.080
There are four entry gates?
And hold on, what's this "annual pass"?

00:02:19.080 --> 00:02:21.160
They charge money just to get in?

00:02:21.160 --> 00:02:23.950
Whoa, there's a 300-minute
wait for a day pass?

00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:27.500
Are you serious? I'm absolutely
terrible about waiting in line.

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:29.000
In fact, I hate it.

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:30.950
That's okay. There's another way.

00:02:30.950 --> 00:02:32.910
--Another way?
--Another way?

00:02:32.910 --> 00:02:34.000
Should be right here.

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:35.660
--A back gate?
--A back gate?

00:02:41.580 --> 00:02:44.580
Confirmed. Please come in.

00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:47.540
Thank you.

00:02:47.540 --> 00:02:48.790
Okay, let's go.

00:02:48.790 --> 00:02:52.080
Huh? Huh? What was that?
What just happened?

00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:54.830
The write-up said that if you have
over 10,000 social media followers,

00:02:54.830 --> 00:02:58.200
you're able to use this back gate.

00:02:58.200 --> 00:03:01.000
Huh? You have 10,000 followers?

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:05.080
It's a dead account that I made long ago.
I guess it had over 10,000 followers.

00:03:05.080 --> 00:03:07.540
Huh?! How did you manage
to get that many followers?

00:03:07.540 --> 00:03:09.290
Oh, there are ways.

00:03:09.290 --> 00:03:13.410
I know. He paid them off.
He doesn't have any friends.

00:03:13.410 --> 00:03:14.540
Did you say something?

00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:17.750
Oh, no. Come on, let's go, Mr. Lonesome.

00:03:17.750 --> 00:03:19.580
--Huh?
--Never mind, never mind, it's all good.

00:03:19.580 --> 00:03:20.750
--Never mind, never mind, it's all good.

00:03:23.370 --> 00:03:25.120
What is this place?

00:03:25.120 --> 00:03:26.120
Huh?

00:03:28.870 --> 00:03:31.790
Huh? Huh? Huh?

00:03:31.790 --> 00:03:35.160
Gentlemen, welcome to Akka Sakka,
the world of dreams and adventure,

00:03:35.160 --> 00:03:39.160
as well as love, hope,
and pure righteous amusement!

00:03:39.160 --> 00:03:43.330
We hope you will sincerely
enjoy your day with us!

00:03:43.330 --> 00:03:44.370
Enjoy?

00:03:44.370 --> 00:03:49.250
♪ Welcome, welcome, dreams, adventure, ♪

00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:52.830
--♪ love, hope, and pure
righteous amusement! ♪

00:03:52.830 --> 00:03:55.950
--I have absolutely no idea how to take this.
--♪ love, hope, and pure
righteous amusement! ♪

00:03:55.950 --> 00:03:57.500
--Same here.
--♪ love, hope, and pure
righteous amusement! ♪

00:03:57.500 --> 00:04:01.660
It says this area is the
"Love and Hope Fantasy Musical Area."

00:04:01.660 --> 00:04:03.200
It looks like awesome fun!

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:04.790
Where do you see that?

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:12.000
Huh? Wh-What?

00:04:13.750 --> 00:04:17.040
♪ Oh, don't be like that ♪

00:04:17.040 --> 00:04:20.200
♪ Come with us to the world of dreams ♪

00:04:20.200 --> 00:04:26.410
♪ Dreaming is a great thing to do ♪

00:04:30.620 --> 00:04:32.580
This is my least favorite thing ever.

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:33.450
--♪ Come, you, too, open the
doorway to love and hope ♪

00:04:33.450 --> 00:04:34.790
--Eh?
--♪ Come, you, too, open the
doorway to love and hope ♪

00:04:34.790 --> 00:04:39.200
--♪ Come, you, too, open the
doorway to love and hope ♪

00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:42.450
♪ Your dreams are just ahead ♪

00:04:42.450 --> 00:04:45.370
--♪ Your dreams will come true ♪

00:04:45.370 --> 00:04:48.870
--Whoa! Hey, what is this, Hatchi?
--♪ Your dreams will come true ♪

00:04:48.870 --> 00:04:51.450
--♪ Dreams, adventure, love, hope ♪
--♪ Dreams, adventure, love, hope ♪

00:04:51.450 --> 00:04:52.040
--Seriously?
--♪ Dreams, adventure, love, hope ♪
--♪ Dreams, adventure, love, hope ♪

00:04:52.040 --> 00:04:52.870
--Seriously?
--♪ pure, righteous ♪
--♪ pure, righteous ♪

00:04:52.870 --> 00:04:55.250
--♪ pure, righteous ♪
--♪ pure, righteous ♪

00:04:55.250 --> 00:04:58.370
--♪ amusement! ♪
--♪ amusement! ♪

00:04:58.370 --> 00:04:59.200
Seriously?

00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:04.830
♪ Why aren't you dancing? ♪

00:05:04.830 --> 00:05:06.410
♪ It's fun! ♪

00:05:06.410 --> 00:05:08.000
--♪ It's fun! ♪
--♪ It's fun! ♪

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:09.580
♪ It's fun! ♪

00:05:09.580 --> 00:05:11.660
--♪ It's fun! ♪
--♪ It's fun! ♪

00:05:11.660 --> 00:05:15.000
These guys are just going to keep
repeating themselves until we do it.

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:17.620
You gotta be kidding me! I'm leaving.

00:05:24.830 --> 00:05:27.250
All right! It's fun!

00:05:27.250 --> 00:05:28.790
♪ It's fun! ♪

00:05:28.790 --> 00:05:32.040
--♪ It's fun! ♪
--♪ It's fun! ♪

00:05:32.040 --> 00:05:34.160
♪ It's fun! ♪

00:05:34.160 --> 00:05:41.330
--♪ It's fun! ♪
--♪ It's fun! ♪

00:05:47.200 --> 00:05:51.200
Okay, on to the next place.
There are all sorts of areas.

00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:52.660
Hold on...

00:05:52.660 --> 00:05:54.410
Give us a minute...

00:05:59.790 --> 00:06:03.450
What is this? Is the whole
planet an amusement park?

00:06:03.450 --> 00:06:05.750
Apparently, each area has a different theme.

00:06:05.750 --> 00:06:09.250
This is the "Fairy Tale
Flower Lovely Play Area."

00:06:09.250 --> 00:06:11.950
Fairy Tale... Flower...?

00:06:11.950 --> 00:06:17.620
They're laying it on thick again,
with "fairy tales," "flowers," <i>and </i>"lovely."

00:06:17.620 --> 00:06:21.160
As long as it's not a musical area,
I'm fine with it.

00:06:21.160 --> 00:06:23.330
I can't take any more of that!

00:06:27.910 --> 00:06:29.330
Eh?

00:06:31.910 --> 00:06:35.450
Huh? Nah, that's not...

00:06:35.450 --> 00:06:37.290
...true at all!

00:06:42.910 --> 00:06:44.790
What is going on around here?

00:06:44.790 --> 00:06:46.700
Yeah, this is getting weird.

00:06:46.700 --> 00:06:50.580
Ah, I forgot to mention this,
but all complaining, abusive language,

00:06:50.580 --> 00:06:53.540
and negative comments are forbidden here.

00:06:53.540 --> 00:06:55.040
--Huh?
--How come?

00:06:55.040 --> 00:06:57.620
Well, this world is one
of dreams and adventure,

00:06:57.620 --> 00:07:01.290
as well as love, hope,
and pure righteous amusement.

00:07:01.290 --> 00:07:02.120
--Huh?
--Huh?

00:07:02.120 --> 00:07:04.580
So, what happens if I say any of that?

00:07:04.580 --> 00:07:07.450
That information isn't provided.

00:07:07.450 --> 00:07:10.700
However, I don't see any garbage
at all on this world, do you?

00:07:12.120 --> 00:07:13.410
--Yeah, you're right about that.

00:07:13.410 --> 00:07:14.750
--Let's go over there next.
--Yeah, you're right about that.

00:07:14.750 --> 00:07:16.870
Ah, okay, let's do that.

00:07:19.330 --> 00:07:20.200
That was fast!

00:07:20.200 --> 00:07:22.160
And there you have it.

00:07:22.160 --> 00:07:24.330
Huh? There I have what?

00:07:24.330 --> 00:07:27.700
Anything dirty is quickly disposed of,
whether things or people.

00:07:27.700 --> 00:07:29.950
Don't make me spell it out.

00:07:31.950 --> 00:07:37.330
Ah, I want to go on this! Let's see,
where is it? Ah, that way! Let's go!

00:07:37.330 --> 00:07:40.290
Jeez, what is going on here?

00:07:41.500 --> 00:07:44.000
This is a hell of a planet we've come to.

00:07:44.000 --> 00:07:47.040
Negative comments are forbidden?
It's full-on purgatory.

00:07:47.040 --> 00:07:49.580
What kind of penalty game is this?

00:07:49.580 --> 00:07:51.040
Huh?

00:07:53.870 --> 00:07:57.120
Wh-What do you want?! Stay away!

00:07:58.160 --> 00:08:04.330
♪ Welcome! Welcome! Dreams!
Adventure! Love! Hope! ♪

00:08:04.330 --> 00:08:06.910
--Shut up, all of you! Stay away from me!
--♪ Pure, righteous amusement! ♪

00:08:06.910 --> 00:08:09.160
--♪ Pure, righteous amusement! ♪

00:08:09.160 --> 00:08:11.750
Stop that, you! I really mean it!

00:08:11.750 --> 00:08:21.580
--♪ It's fun! ♪
--♪ It's fun! ♪

00:08:21.580 --> 00:08:25.200
A-All right! I'm having fun, too!

00:08:31.250 --> 00:08:33.580
A fully-grown adult on the teacups?

00:08:33.580 --> 00:08:35.250
Are you sure you should say that?

00:08:35.250 --> 00:08:36.910
This is something little kids ride on

00:08:36.910 --> 00:08:38.910
during the first three months
after they start dating.

00:08:38.910 --> 00:08:42.500
Only couples ride on this, saying
"This is as happy as I can be."

00:08:42.500 --> 00:08:44.080
Cool it, Robby.

00:08:44.080 --> 00:08:48.540
I'm just saying, I get motion sick easily.

00:08:50.040 --> 00:08:53.950
Robby if you value your life, then seriously,
seriously, seriously, hold it in.

00:08:53.950 --> 00:08:55.330
Huh? O-Oh, yeah...

00:08:55.330 --> 00:08:57.700
Nice! I love these things!

00:08:57.700 --> 00:09:02.290
Fairy tales are great, and I don't
get motion sickness at all!

00:09:02.290 --> 00:09:06.450
--In that case, off you go! Lovely!
--In that case, off you go! Lovely!

00:09:09.250 --> 00:09:11.160
Whoa! What is this?!

00:09:11.160 --> 00:09:12.580
Lovely! Fun!

00:09:12.580 --> 00:09:15.540
Screw this! Teacups are
for drinking tea out of!

00:09:15.540 --> 00:09:20.160
They're not for sitting in and
spinning around! Stop! Quit it! Hey!

00:09:21.950 --> 00:09:25.000
Welcome to the Lovely Flower Treasure Box!

00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:27.870
Find your own treasure box of the heart, too!

00:09:27.870 --> 00:09:28.700
--Okay, off you go to find dreams,
hope, and adventure! Lovely!

00:09:28.700 --> 00:09:31.870
--W-We're so high! Hey!
This is definitely out of the question!
--Okay, off you go to find dreams,
hope, and adventure! Lovely!

00:09:31.870 --> 00:09:33.660
--Get me the hell down from here!
--Okay, off you go to find dreams,
hope, and adventure! Lovely!

00:09:33.660 --> 00:09:34.910
Down you go.

00:09:45.700 --> 00:09:47.410
--Whoa...
--Eh?

00:09:47.410 --> 00:09:49.160
Is this...?

00:09:51.290 --> 00:09:52.870
What fun!

00:09:52.870 --> 00:09:54.830
--Barf-making lovely!
--Barf-making lovely!

00:09:54.830 --> 00:09:56.790
What fun!

00:09:56.790 --> 00:09:59.700
Come on, you two, it's lovely smile time!

00:09:59.700 --> 00:10:02.160
--Lovely...
--Lovely...

00:10:02.160 --> 00:10:04.330
Wow, this turned out great!

00:10:04.330 --> 00:10:06.700
Hey, let's go over there next!

00:10:06.700 --> 00:10:10.120
Actually, let's take a breather, Hatchi.

00:10:10.120 --> 00:10:11.830
But in just a little while,

00:10:11.830 --> 00:10:15.750
the Akka Sakka Lovely Fantastic
Fairy Tale Dream Parade begins!

00:10:15.750 --> 00:10:20.870
An over-the-top-named parade, right?
I'm getting used to that.

00:10:20.870 --> 00:10:23.330
Besides, we have to claim
our spot to watch the parade,

00:10:23.330 --> 00:10:25.290
so we have to go on lots of other rides first.

00:10:25.290 --> 00:10:27.120
--Go on others?
--Go on others?

00:10:27.120 --> 00:10:29.540
Wait, you said claim a spot?

00:10:29.540 --> 00:10:32.580
Mm-hmm. I've never been
to a place like this before,

00:10:32.580 --> 00:10:34.410
but it sure is fun, isn't it?

00:10:34.410 --> 00:10:36.580
Come on, let's go!

00:10:36.580 --> 00:10:39.910
Damn that Hatchi. He's so
carried away, he's skipping.

00:10:39.910 --> 00:10:44.580
Also, this is his first time at an
amusement park? That's surprising.

00:10:44.580 --> 00:10:47.040
He's probably spent all his time studying.

00:10:47.040 --> 00:10:50.750
Come on, hurry!

00:10:50.750 --> 00:10:53.870
He really is just a kid.

00:10:53.870 --> 00:10:56.040
Yeah, well, what choice do we have?

00:10:56.040 --> 00:10:58.580
You got it.

00:10:58.580 --> 00:11:00.830
Ugh, this is rough.

00:11:00.830 --> 00:11:03.620
Lovely, lovely, super-lovely!

00:11:05.410 --> 00:11:07.040
Mr. Yang, bad news!

00:11:07.040 --> 00:11:08.910
It's a 500-minute wait for a day pass!

00:11:08.910 --> 00:11:10.870
How many hours is 500 minutes?

00:11:10.870 --> 00:11:14.750
Let's see, one hour is 60 minutes,
so two hours is 120 minutes,

00:11:14.750 --> 00:11:17.080
three hours is an additional 60 minutes...

00:11:17.080 --> 00:11:19.700
You idiot! It's eight hours and 20 minutes!

00:11:19.700 --> 00:11:21.870
--Leave it to Mr. Yang to count fast!
--Leave it to Mr. Yang to count fast!

00:11:21.870 --> 00:11:24.870
Money will solve this problem. Let's go.

00:11:24.870 --> 00:11:26.250
That's our Mr. Yang!

00:11:26.250 --> 00:11:27.750
That's him, all right!

00:11:30.620 --> 00:11:34.000
There's still over two hours
before the parade, right?

00:11:34.000 --> 00:11:35.910
Are there already this many people waiting?

00:11:35.910 --> 00:11:39.200
It's so they'll have better seats
to watch from, so of course!

00:11:39.200 --> 00:11:43.290
Hey, Ikku, what's wrong?
You haven't said anything for a while.

00:11:43.290 --> 00:11:47.250
I mean, if I do talk, I'll just say
something that causes trouble, right?

00:11:47.250 --> 00:11:49.370
Like right now, I want nothing
more than to make a crack

00:11:49.370 --> 00:11:51.540
about that rose treasure box
hanging from Hatchi's shoulder,

00:11:51.540 --> 00:11:53.870
filled with caramel popcorn.

00:11:53.870 --> 00:11:59.120
Oh, this? It's actually called a
Lovely Flower Dream Treasure Caramel Box.

00:11:59.120 --> 00:12:02.950
It has strawberry caramel popcorn inside.
Once I finish eating this,

00:12:02.950 --> 00:12:05.080
I can add another serving's worth.

00:12:05.080 --> 00:12:09.450
O-Oh, yeah? Th-That sounds lovely.

00:12:09.450 --> 00:12:12.250
I've eaten it all. I'm going
to go buy some more.

00:12:12.250 --> 00:12:14.750
Okay, we'll be waiting lovely here for you.

00:12:14.750 --> 00:12:17.540
Mm-hmm! Thanks for lovely saving my place!

00:12:19.370 --> 00:12:22.950
Tonight is the once-a-year
"Lovely Star Night," you know.

00:12:22.950 --> 00:12:26.290
I wonder who this year's
Lovely King and Queen will be.

00:12:26.290 --> 00:12:29.000
The two of us are going to be the ones

00:12:29.000 --> 00:12:31.870
who ring the Lovely Bell in the
Fairy Tale Lovely Fantasy Castle!

00:12:31.870 --> 00:12:34.830
My! How lovely fantastic!

00:12:34.830 --> 00:12:37.410
Lovely Star Night?

00:12:37.410 --> 00:12:40.910
What is this? There sure are
a lot of couples here.

00:12:40.910 --> 00:12:45.450
Mr. Yang, tonight is the
once-a-year "Lovely Star Night."

00:12:45.450 --> 00:12:47.040
What is that?

00:12:47.040 --> 00:12:50.290
Lovely Star Night is a
hyper-miraculous phenomenon,

00:12:50.290 --> 00:12:53.750
when the planetoids near Akka Sakka overlap,

00:12:53.750 --> 00:12:56.500
and their light shines in the shape of a heart.

00:12:56.500 --> 00:12:59.700
Legend says that on this night,
when the Lovely King and Queen are chosen,

00:12:59.700 --> 00:13:03.000
and they ring the Lovely Bell
in the Fairy Tale Lovely Fantasy Castle,

00:13:03.000 --> 00:13:07.290
they will be bound together forever!

00:13:07.290 --> 00:13:13.370
Bound forever? Hmph, Robby,
the time has come at last

00:13:13.370 --> 00:13:16.080
when you and I will be bound together.

00:13:19.750 --> 00:13:22.790
I got chocolate caramel popcorn this time.

00:13:24.200 --> 00:13:26.200
Huh?

00:13:26.200 --> 00:13:29.540
Huh? Huh? Huh? Huh?

00:13:29.540 --> 00:13:33.120
Robby!

00:13:36.040 --> 00:13:38.330
Robby? Ikku?

00:13:38.330 --> 00:13:39.620
Where are you?

00:13:49.580 --> 00:13:51.700
What fun!

00:13:59.910 --> 00:14:02.540
Are you lovely all right?

00:14:05.870 --> 00:14:08.040
Attention, ladies and gentlemen.

00:14:08.040 --> 00:14:10.750
--Paging Mr. Robby Yarge,
Mr. Robby Yarge, from Earth.

00:14:10.750 --> 00:14:13.160
--Hey, Robby, they're calling you.
--Paging Mr. Robby Yarge,
Mr. Robby Yarge, from Earth.

00:14:13.160 --> 00:14:15.330
--Huh? Me?
--A boy in his teens, roughly 180 cm tall,

00:14:15.330 --> 00:14:21.750
with a rose treasure popcorn box
slung across his body, is calling for you.

00:14:21.750 --> 00:14:23.620
--That's Hatchi!
--That's Hatchi!

00:14:23.620 --> 00:14:26.450
Mr. Yang, I think I just
heard Robby being paged.

00:14:26.450 --> 00:14:28.750
That was definitely him! Mr. Yang!

00:14:28.750 --> 00:14:32.120
Yeah, I positively heard it, myself.

00:14:32.120 --> 00:14:34.450
Where is the lost child center?!

00:14:40.790 --> 00:14:45.290
Hey, buddy, you can't tell them
your name or where you live?

00:14:45.290 --> 00:14:46.370
Pretty much.

00:14:46.370 --> 00:14:47.910
You're so lame.

00:14:47.910 --> 00:14:51.450
Hey, you're lost, too.
You're pretty lame, yourself.

00:14:51.450 --> 00:14:55.540
Unlike you, buddy, I got lost on purpose.

00:14:55.540 --> 00:14:57.910
I'm also not giving my name
or address, on purpose.

00:14:57.910 --> 00:15:00.910
I'm sure my SPs are
panicking right about now.

00:15:00.910 --> 00:15:02.160
SPs?

00:15:02.160 --> 00:15:05.540
Yeah. My mom and dad are both busy people,

00:15:05.540 --> 00:15:09.250
so my playmates are always security police.

00:15:09.250 --> 00:15:12.870
As you can see, I am quite well off.

00:15:12.870 --> 00:15:16.330
That's why I always have grown-ups
at my side fussing over me.

00:15:16.330 --> 00:15:19.540
It's nice to get away and
be alone once in a while, huh?

00:15:28.370 --> 00:15:31.160
Buddy, who did you get separated from?

00:15:31.160 --> 00:15:33.870
Your father? Your mother?

00:15:33.870 --> 00:15:39.620
No. Ever since I was a little,
my parents were never close to me.

00:15:39.620 --> 00:15:40.580
Huh?

00:15:40.580 --> 00:15:44.200
But then, once I took the
plunge and went outside,

00:15:44.200 --> 00:15:47.000
I've had some really surprising encounters.

00:15:48.040 --> 00:15:51.290
Hey, Hatchi, you here?

00:15:51.290 --> 00:15:54.910
Oh, there you are! What the hell
are you paging me for?

00:15:54.910 --> 00:15:57.790
Getting called out in the middle
of the park is embarrassing as hell--

00:15:57.790 --> 00:16:00.580
I mean, lovely as hell, you know.

00:16:00.580 --> 00:16:02.410
You took enough time. I've been waiting.

00:16:02.410 --> 00:16:03.910
Huh?

00:16:03.910 --> 00:16:05.910
You should stop always
feeling sorry for yourself

00:16:05.910 --> 00:16:11.080
and go out and make friends, too.
Just don't worry them too much.

00:16:14.250 --> 00:16:16.410
Hey, hold on, Hatchi!

00:16:16.410 --> 00:16:20.870
I came to pick you up, and you
don't even say thanks? Come on!

00:16:20.870 --> 00:16:22.620
Friends...?

00:16:28.040 --> 00:16:32.290
Damn it, I don't want you getting lost
and having me paged again.

00:16:32.290 --> 00:16:34.330
--I-I didn't exactly get lost.
I was just tired, and needed to rest.

00:16:34.330 --> 00:16:35.620
--Ladies and gentlemen!
--I-I didn't exactly get lost.
I was just tired, and needed to rest.

00:16:35.620 --> 00:16:37.290
--The Lovely Fantastic Fairy Tale
Dream Parade is beginning!
--I-I didn't exactly get lost.
I was just tired, and needed to rest.

00:16:37.290 --> 00:16:38.750
--The Lovely Fantastic Fairy Tale
Dream Parade is beginning!
--They even gave me a drink.

00:16:38.750 --> 00:16:41.580
-The Lovely Fantastic Fairy Tale
Dream Parade is beginning!
--What's going on?

00:16:41.580 --> 00:16:43.120
We've been lovely waiting for this!

00:16:43.120 --> 00:16:46.370
It's fantastic dream exciting lovely!

00:16:46.370 --> 00:16:50.120
You two seem to be fitting in
on this world now.

00:16:50.120 --> 00:16:51.790
Yeah, well...

00:16:51.790 --> 00:16:54.700
Seeing how much fun you
were having playing here,

00:16:54.700 --> 00:16:57.580
I thought it wasn't so bad
being a kid once in a while.

00:16:57.580 --> 00:16:59.250
--Huh?
--Just saying, it's likely that being forced
to say all these positive things,

00:16:59.250 --> 00:17:01.660
--Just saying, it's likely that being forced
to say all these positive things,

00:17:01.660 --> 00:17:04.790
it seems my brain really
has been turned lovely.

00:17:04.790 --> 00:17:08.620
Me, too! Don't have a brain, though. Lovely!

00:17:08.620 --> 00:17:11.450
Okay, let's enjoy the parade.

00:17:11.450 --> 00:17:13.040
Mm-hmm.

00:17:13.040 --> 00:17:15.160
Hey, where is Robby Yarge?

00:17:15.160 --> 00:17:16.790
He was just paged here, right?

00:17:16.790 --> 00:17:21.160
He would have come to pick up
a 180-cm-tall teenage boy!

00:17:21.160 --> 00:17:22.250
Should have!

00:17:22.250 --> 00:17:24.620
Oh, him? He already left.

00:17:24.620 --> 00:17:26.080
What?!

00:17:26.080 --> 00:17:29.700
Lovely as hell! Fairy tale as hell!
Fantastic as hell!

00:17:29.700 --> 00:17:30.620
Here it comes!

00:17:30.620 --> 00:17:32.200
--Lovely!
--Lovely!

00:17:32.200 --> 00:17:33.790
--Fantastic!
--Fantastic!

00:17:33.790 --> 00:17:35.500
--Dreaming!
--Dreaming!

00:17:35.500 --> 00:17:37.080
--Fairy tale!
--Fairy tale!

00:17:37.080 --> 00:17:38.700
--Dreaming!
--Dreaming!

00:17:38.700 --> 00:17:39.540
Fairy tale!

00:17:39.540 --> 00:17:41.120
--Fairy tale!
--Fairy tale!

00:17:41.120 --> 00:17:42.580
--Lovely!
--Lovely!

00:17:42.580 --> 00:17:43.750
Fantastic!

00:17:43.750 --> 00:17:45.450
--Fantastic?!
--Fantastic?!

00:17:45.450 --> 00:17:46.870
Yikes! It's him!

00:17:46.870 --> 00:17:48.500
Robby, hurry! Let's get out of here!

00:17:48.500 --> 00:17:50.200
Okay, to the spaceship!

00:17:50.200 --> 00:17:52.540
No! Yang is over that way!

00:17:52.540 --> 00:17:55.080
In that case, I'll go get the
<i>Nagaya Voyager </i>ready to launch.

00:17:55.080 --> 00:17:57.870
You guys run and find a place
where I can pick you up.

00:17:57.870 --> 00:17:59.410
Yeah! Please do, Ikku!

00:17:59.410 --> 00:18:01.040
Let's go! And don't get lost!

00:18:01.040 --> 00:18:03.040
<i>You're </i>the one who got lost!

00:18:03.040 --> 00:18:04.290
Mr. Yang, over there!

00:18:04.290 --> 00:18:05.410
It's Robby!

00:18:05.410 --> 00:18:08.080
After him!

00:18:08.080 --> 00:18:09.290
--Lovely!
--Lovely!

00:18:09.290 --> 00:18:10.410
--Fantastic!
--Fantastic!

00:18:10.410 --> 00:18:11.620
--Dreaming!
--Dreaming!

00:18:11.620 --> 00:18:12.790
--Fairy tale!
--Fairy tale!

00:18:12.790 --> 00:18:14.160
--Dreaming!
--Dreaming!

00:18:14.160 --> 00:18:16.370
Run up to the highest level of the castle!

00:18:16.370 --> 00:18:18.200
Yeah!

00:18:18.200 --> 00:18:19.950
Mr. Yang! The stairs!

00:18:19.950 --> 00:18:21.250
We can't make it with the float!

00:18:21.250 --> 00:18:23.750
Of course not! Set us down at once!

00:18:23.750 --> 00:18:27.370
Mr. Yang, Robby and the
Lovely Bell are up these stairs!

00:18:27.370 --> 00:18:29.040
I know!

00:18:31.040 --> 00:18:35.790
Yes! As long as I'm catching Robby,
I'll ring the bell with him!

00:18:35.790 --> 00:18:39.580
Two birds with one stone!
Two wins for the price of one! Victory!

00:18:39.580 --> 00:18:41.700
Mr. Yang, good luck to you!

00:18:41.700 --> 00:18:44.580
Ring that bell together with him!

00:18:44.580 --> 00:18:47.330
Ladies and gentlemen,
look up into the night sky!

00:18:47.330 --> 00:18:50.450
A miraculous astronomical phenomenon
that happens only once a year,

00:18:50.450 --> 00:18:53.950
the Akka Sakka Star Night, is now beginning!

00:18:56.120 --> 00:18:57.700
And the moment you've been waiting for--

00:18:57.700 --> 00:19:02.910
this year's Akka Sakka Lovely King
and Queen have been chosen!

00:19:04.580 --> 00:19:09.450
I will be the one who
rings this bell, with Robby!

00:19:09.450 --> 00:19:13.290
